CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 6
Obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children are the shared responsibility of:
a. regional government;
b. society;
c. family;
d. parents; and
e. non-governmental institutions including Customary Institutions and Business Entities.

Article 3
The regulation of the fundamentals of PPA implementation aims to:
a. prevent acts of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children;
b. eliminate all forms of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades the dignity and honor of women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services to women and children who are victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

Article 5
Child victims of acts of violence, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades human dignity and worth, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 4, also obtain special rights, as follows:
a. Right to respect and full utilization for survival, growth and development;
b. Right to basic services;
c. Right to equal protection;
d. Right to be free from various stigma;
e. Right to employment;
f. Right to decent housing and livable environment;
g. Right to Women's empowerment; and
h. Right to prevention of violence.

CHAPTER IV
DUTIES OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 11
The Regional Government has the duty to undertake prevention, handling and recovery efforts for victims of violence against Women and Children, by:
a. collecting data and information about Women and Children Victims of acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades human dignity and worth;
b. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to PPA;
c. providing education about anti-violence values in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades human dignity and worth against women and children;
d. conducting prevention of child marriage;
e. providing rehabilitation facilities; and
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation regarding PPA against acts of violence in various forms, exploitation, discrimination, mistreatment and/or treatment that degrades human dignity and worth.

